# ─── Required in production ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Encrypts provider access tokens at rest (AES-256-GCM). Without it, Kroner
# refuses to store any provider credential — demo mode still works.
# Generate:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# PostgreSQL connection string. Supabase, RDS, Neon, or a local server.
# Leave unset for local development: Kroner then runs an embedded Postgres
# under .data/, with the identical schema, migrations and RLS policies.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/kroner

# Public origin, used to build the bank authorization redirect.
# APP_URL=https://kroner.example.com

# ─── AI assistant (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without a key the assistant still answers, using a rule-based intent parser
# over the same read-only queries. The numbers are identical either way.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5

# ─── Open Banking: GoCardless Bank Account Data (optional) ─────────────────
# Free tier at https://bankaccountdata.gocardless.com — covers Danish banks.
# The consent flow is hosted by GoCardless and your bank; Kroner never sees
# MitID, a bank password, or any other authentication factor.
# GOCARDLESS_SECRET_ID=
# GOCARDLESS_SECRET_KEY=
# GOCARDLESS_BASE_URL=https://bankaccountdata.gocardless.com/api/v2

# Swap the Open Banking aggregator without touching anything else.
# BANK_PROVIDER=gocardless

# ─── Stripe (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ONE-TAP: Stripe Connect OAuth, requested with scope=read_only. The user
# approves in Stripe and never copies a key. Stripe enforces the read-only
# scope server-side, so the restriction does not depend on this app behaving.
# Create a Connect platform at https://dashboard.stripe.com/settings/connect
# and add https://your-domain/api/stripe/callback as a redirect URI.
# STRIPE_CONNECT_CLIENT_ID=ca_...
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...

# FALLBACK: a RESTRICTED key (rk_live_…) with read access to Balance
# transactions and Charges, pasted in the UI. Encrypted and stored per user;
# this variable is only a default for single-tenant deployments.
# STRIPE_API_KEY=

# ─── MobilePay ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Personal MobilePay needs NOTHING here. There is no consumer API and there
# never has been; those payments arrive through the bank feed, and Kroner
# reads them back out with the counterparty's name. Connect a bank and the
# MobilePay screen fills in by itself.
#
# These are for the MERCHANT side only — a Vipps MobilePay business agreement.
# MOBILEPAY_CLIENT_ID=
# MOBILEPAY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# MOBILEPAY_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY=

# ─── Prepared, not yet wired ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
# PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ─── Bookkeeping export (architecture in place, mapping required) ──────────
# DINERO_CLIENT_ID=
# DINERO_CLIENT_SECRET=
# BILLY_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# ECONOMIC_APP_SECRET_TOKEN=
# ECONOMIC_AGREEMENT_TOKEN=

# ─── Tuning ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EMBEDDED_DB_DIR=.data/pgdata
# PGPOOL_MAX=10
